  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-1998-p13.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Extend the figure to a \\(4\\) by \\(4\\) grid as shown:\n\nThe large square consists of \\(16\\) unit squares. The shaded square is made from four half-unit squares, so its area is \\(4\\cdot\\dfrac{1}{2}=2.\\) Therefore, the required ratio is \\(\\dfrac{2}{16}=\\dfrac{1}{8}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C .",
      "hints": [
        "Extend the grid lines in the large square.",
        "The shaded square is made from four half-unit squares."
      ],
